      "id": "at-glance",
      "title": "At a glance",
      "body": "For travelers, Phòng này nóng quá is the phrase to keep ready for \"This room is too hot\" in front desk, room, check-in, and hotel-service moments. This is for when the room temperature is the main problem. Lead with the room problem before asking for the fix. It works best when you focus on naming the room problem first so staff can send help or offer a fix. After you say it, listen for a room-number check, maintenance visit, new key, or room-change option; the next rows help you keep the exchange moving.",
